   Responsibility, Istanbul, TURKEY, MAR 18-19, 2010},
Organization = {German Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; IMRE Alumni Network},
Abstract = {Through an empirical study on the chain retailers from 35 cities in
   China, the authors find out that the current economic development level
   has a negative impact on the development of department stores, although
   department stores still play an important part in the market. Since
   logistics become increasingly more important for chain retailers, per
   capita area of roads has distinctively positive effects on the
   development of both supermarkets and the convenience stores. Meanwhile,
   the authors stress that the development of specialty store relies
   largely on urban environmental and economic development level.},
