   (ICEEP 2013), Guilin, PEOPLES R CHINA, APR 19-21, 2013},
Organization = {Inner Mongolia Univ; Chinese Acad Sci, Res Ctr Eco Environm Sci, Key Lab
   Environm Biotechnol},
Abstract = {Alkanes are widespread in nature and cause seriously pollution of
   environment. In many of oil pollution treatment method, because of
   economic, effective and less damaging to the environment and many other
   advantages, bioremediation technology is thought to have broad
   application prospects. In this study, we isolated an efficient
   alkane-degrading strain from some coal gasification wastewater sludge.
   It was identified the strain L2-4 as Acinetobacter sp.(KC211013) through
   morphology and 16SrDNA sequence analysis. The maximum degradation rate
   was aquired to 58.7\% under the condition of original alkanes
   concentration 700mg/L, pH 7.0 and temperature 35 degrees C. The study
   was designed to provide good strain resources for oil pollution
   remediation and microbial en hanced oil recovery.},
