   ROMANIA, NOV 26-28, 2009},
Abstract = {The article presents information regarding values ( which can be
   relational, material, professional, psycho-moral and emotional) that are
   considered by parents as being important for their children. It is
   important to be aware of the educational and cultural consumption
   activities which are associated with these values. We are referring to
   the activities that parents suggest to their children: reading, working,
   taking part in religious activities, games. The information has been
   obtained through exploratory research, done on a group of 260 families
   from the urban and rural environment, that have at least one child
   between the ages of 7 and 11. We believe that the information is
   important in order to shape educational strategies which are addressed
   to parents as well as children.},
