Abstract = {In this paper some results obtained in the SICURO research project
   carried out by the Laboratory for Transport Systems Analysis (LAST) of
   Mediterranea University of Reggio Calabria (Italy) are presented.
   Microscopic models able to simulate supply and demand-supply interaction
   of a road transportation system in emergency conditions are described. A
   microscopic link model (car-following) is specified and calibrated.
   Parameters are calibrated from data observed during a real simulation of
   evacuation executed in the test site of Melito Porto Salvo (Italy). A
   computer application is performed in order to reproduce the evacuation
   phases observed. Some indicators for testing the performance of a road
   transportation network in emergency conditions are defined and
   estimated.},
