   Antalya, TURKEY, MAY 25-29, 2011},
Abstract = {During the psychotherapeutic work I have encountered profound issues
   related to the mother's lack of bounding with the fetus, prenatal
   abandonment, mother's rejection of the fetus, various forms of
   aggression (e. g., single or multiple abortion attempts, domestic
   violence), which led to prenatal traumas. For activation of such traumas
   I metaphorically reconstruct within the group therapy the context of
   prenatal life, using different forms of experiential ``provocative{''}
   exercises. The person gets in contact with emotions from the prenatal
   period such us fear, angry or very deep sadness. These emotions were
   always related with mother's lack of bounding with the fetus in
   different forms or even to the unknown situations that were perceived as
   dangerous for the fetus's life. (C) 2011 Published by Elsevier Ltd.
