Note = {3rd International Conference on Green Materials and Environmental
   Engineering (GMEE), Beijing, PEOPLES R CHINA, OCT 22-22, 2017},
Abstract = {Urbanization is the objective demand of narrowing the gap between urban
   and rural areas and building a harmonious society. With the concept of
   sustainability to promote the healthy urban development, urbanization is
   estimated by a comprehensive evaluation system instead of single
   indicator method. The study, which constructs a comprehensive evaluation
   index system consisting of 19 indicators, adopts the composite index
   method and takes 289 prefecture-level cities of China in 2014 as the
   sample. Firstly, the paper studies the correlation and overlap
   information between indicator variables based on factor analysis. Then,
   a structural equation model is established by the Amos software to check
   out the results of factor analysis. The result shows that the fitting of
   model is good. The path coefficients are calculated and the weight of
   indicators is determined. Finally, the comprehensive urbanization score
   and ranking of China's 289 prefecture-level cities are calculated, and
   the spatial difference of urbanization level in China is analyzed.},
