Abstract = {Advancements regarding Dynamic Traffic Assignment (DTA) microscopic
   models for the simulation of supply and demand-supply interaction of a
   road transportation system in emergency conditions are presented. They
   are related to link and node models specified in the research project
   SICURO, carried out by the Laboratory for Transport Systems Analysis
   (LAST) of the Mediterranea University of Reggio Calabria (Italy).
   Microscopic link (car-following) and gap-acceptance (rejection) models
   for non-signalized intersections are calibrated from data observed
   during a real simulation of evacuation. An application is performed in
   order to reproduce the observed evacuation phases through a set of
   performance indicators.},
