Abstract = {The concentration of hydrogen peroxide (H2O2) in rainwater samples
   collected between April 2003 and April 2004 in downtown Sao Paulo were
   determined. The concentrations of H2O2 ranged from 2.29 to 48.6 mu mol
   L-1, with an average value (n = 70) of 13.1 (+/- 11.3) mu mol L-1. The
   higher concentrations were observed in spring and summer. The
   volume-weighted mean (VWM) of the free H+ was 6.5 mu mol L-1,
   corresponding to a pH of 5.2. The analysisOf SO42-, NO3-, and HCOO-, in
   the same set of samples, showed an average concentration of 11.7 (+/-
   10.9), 20.0 ( +/- 18.0), and 6.18 ( +/- 12.4) mu mol L-1, respectively.
   The HCOO- concentrations showed correlation (r = 0.43) with H2O2,which
   can indicate reactions in aqueous phase where these two species are
   formed.},
