Abstract = {Single NGO cannot play important roles in influencing public decision
   making. In this paper, the authors provide a new strategy of
   cooperation, that is, environmental Non-Governmental Organizations
   (ENGOs) as a leader should work together with other NGOs. In order to
   select right partners, a series of selecting indices are picked up,
   while the evaluating method which is based on the grey relational
   analysis (GRA) is established. Then, practices of the research results
   based on a Chinese urban mass transit project were discussed. The paper
   provides a general mechanism for improving the effectiveness of NGOs
   through public participation.},
