   Univ; New York Acad Sci; European Soc Cognit Sci Music},
Abstract = {The goal of the present study was to determine whether relaxing music
   (as compared to silence) might facilitate recovery from a
   psychologically stressful task. To this aim, changes in salivary
   cortisol levels were regularly monitored in 24 students before and after
   the Trier Social Stress Test. The data show that in the presence of
   music, the salivary cortisol level ceased to increase after the
   stressor, whereas in silence it continued to increase for 30 minutes.},
