Abstract = {We performed two parallel interview studies of stroke patients (n = 20)
   and professional nurses (n = 5) to gain more insight into the
   therapeutic role of music listening in stroke rehabilitation. Results
   suggest that music listening can be used to relax, improve mood, and
   provide both physical and mental activation during the early stages of
   recovery from stroke. Thus, music listening could provide a useful
   clinical tool in stroke rehabilitation.},
