   Acid Reign 95, GOTHENBURG, SWEDEN, JUN 26-30, 1995},
Organization = {Swedish Environm Protect Agcy; Swedish Environm Res Inst; Provincial
   Govt Goteborg; Provincial Govt Bohus Ian},
Abstract = {This work investigates the response of porous carbonate building stones
   to acid deposition during a short-term exposure period and the
   characteristics that influence their reactivity and/or durability.
   Several carbonate porous stones used in Spanish and English monuments
   were exposed to English urban and suburban environments. In each
   location they were both exposed to and sheltered from rainfall. Monthly
   analyses were carried out in order to investigate any possible sign of
   reaction. In addition, some physical properties of the stones relating
   to transfer of moisture were determined. Results indicate that the
   reactivity of these stones is relatively high, significant signs of
   reaction were detected within only a few months of exposure. Under the
   same environmental conditions, the response and reactivity of porous
   carbonate stones are determined by their petrophysical characteristics.},
