   Putrajaya, MALAYSIA, MAR 05-06, 2013},
Organization = {Univ Tenaga Nas (UNITEN)},
Abstract = {This paper presents energy flow models developed to estimate technical
   losses in distribution network. Energy flow models applied in this paper
   is based on input energy and peak demand of distribution network, feeder
   length and peak demand, transformer loading capacity, and load factor.
   Two case studies, an urban distribution network and a rural distribution
   network are used to illustrate application of the energy flow models.
   Results on technical losses obtained for the two distribution networks
   are consistent and comparable to network of similar types and
   characteristics. Hence, the energy flow models are suitable for
   practical application.},
