   \& Remote Sensing Soc},
Abstract = {Water leak detection in water transportation mains outside urban areas
   by airborne remote sensing has been assessed with a series of
   measurement campaigns in 2017 and 2018 over SCP (Societe du Canal de
   Provence - France) network. The most appropriate equipment for revealing
   high moisture areas and artificial leaks coming from the image database
   (VNIR, TIR spectral range) allowed us to validate the choice of the
   onboard instrumentation for both types of platforms (manned \& unmanned)
   associated with the multispectral approach (Triangle method). This work
   aims to validate further the water leak detection technique developed in
   the WADI project. This was performed in the framework of a new airborne
   campaign in May and September 2019 over EDIA (Empresa de Desenvolvimento
   e Infra-estruturas do Alqueva - Portugal) network with a plane and an
   UAV in operational environment.},
